      decl_name: "diagnostics_for_consumer",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "qualified_callee_in_call_position_resolves",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "qualified_callee_in_pipe_position_resolves",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "dotted_pipe_callee_without_application_is_method_then_field",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "bare_callee_in_pipe_position_is_unchanged",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST RATHER THAN A .dag WITNESS, and it is a REACHABILITY limit rather than a preference: the two builtins a .dag witness would use for this subject -- compile_dag_rust_emit_check and compile_dag_diagnostic_census -- both resolve their synthetic source through v1_compiler.cli_run build_module_path_index_from_witness_roots, which walks the live tree. A witness written on either declares ReadsLiveTree and is therefore DECLINED by the required floor's home policy rather than executed, which DESIGN's CI section already records for the compile-clean witness family: discovered, counted, and answering nothing. Authoring one more such witness would add a name to that family without adding an assertion that runs, which DESIGN 4b calls worse than absent because it is cited as coverage. compile_sources takes its sources in memory, so the evidence here reads no repository file and needs no module index -- it is hermetic by construction, and it executes today under cargo test.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM: cargo test is a LOCAL check in this repository, removed from CI by operator ruling 2026-07-11. So this evidence executes on demand and is not a merge gate, and no gate closes this class until a required phase emits over a closure -- the compile re-add DESIGN names as this class's restoration trigger. Stating that here rather than letting the row imply CI coverage is the point of writing it down.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE -- does the change serve the v2 self-host program. Under namespace-only resolution every callee becomes qualified, so a qualified callee in pipe position moves from rare to ordinary; the branch measured this class at roughly 119 of its 410 diagnostics. A parser that answers one denotation two ways by position is a direct tax on that program.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +7, all seven citable above and enumerated rather than counted, all seven in the ONE new file. src/v1/02_parse.dag is a .dag change and adds no hand item; its Rust mirror is generated, so its disposition is generated-surface regeneration and listing it would net a generated change into a hand census.\n\nA PARAGRAPH WAS REMOVED FROM THIS ROW AND THE REMOVAL IS RECORDED RATHER THAN MADE SILENTLY, because a census receipt that quietly changes what it claims is worse than one that was wrong once. An earlier revision of this row excluded six declarations in src/v1/stage0/src/bin/infer_semantics_witness.rs -- empty_type_env and five optional-match and resolve probes -- as ExistingSeedItemModified, each having gained one authored_import_names initializer. THAT PARAGRAPH IS NOW FALSE AND IS DELETED: the file has NO diff in this change, and origin/main already carries all six initializers. Main repaired them independently, and this branch's copy of the repair was dropped when a merge produced the field TWICE per literal -- main added it after module_path, this branch after source_visible_names, and git's text merge kept both (E0062 at six sites). Keeping main's placement removed this change's delta in that file entirely. So the exclusion paragraph described BASE-BRANCH work as part of this change, which makes a hand-Rust census receipt inaccurate in the one direction that matters -- it inflates what the change is answerable for. Found by review 56100.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE EVIDENCE, since the deleted paragraph also carried a live fact: the enumerated evidence could not execute at all while those six initializers were missing, because cargo builds a crate's bins for a --test target too. It executes now. The repair that made it executable is MAIN's, not this change's, and saying so is the point of correcting the row rather than deleting the sentence.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all seven when a required phase compiles a multi-module closure from fixture-authored sources -- the compile re-add on the queue the floor cut created. At that point the same four cases are authorable as .dag witnesses over in-memory sources and execute in the floor, so the assertions move to the substrate unchanged and the Rust file is redundant rather than merely unfashionable. What does NOT dissolve them is the single-source compile builtins gaining a second caller: those read the live tree, so a witness on them is declined and would retire executing evidence in favour of a name. What does NOT dissolve them either is this defect being fixed -- the fix is what they guard.",
  current_boundary: "src/v1/02_parse.dag parse_pipe_rhs; src/v1/02_parse.dag parse_pipe_callee_rest; src/v1/02_parse.dag pipe_callee_path_is_applied; src/v1/stage0/tests/qualified_callee_pipe_position.rs; dag/gunbc/qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth.dag"
}
